  "result": "Done! I've implemented the VAT report functionality:\n\n**Added `vatSummary(invoices)` to src/reports.js:**\n- Returns array with one entry per VAT rate: [{ rate, base, vat }]\n- **Filter criteria:**\n  - Includes invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'\n  - Excludes draft invoices\n- **Calculations per line:**\n  - base = lineTotal - lineDiscount (line amount after discount applied)\n  - vat = base \u00d7 (vatRate / 100), rounded per line using roundCents()\n- **Aggregation:**\n  - Sums base and vat across all lines in all filtered invoices\n  - Groups by VAT rate\n  - All amounts clamped to \u2265 0\n- **Sorting:** By rate descending (21, 9, 0)\n\n**Added 14 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Empty invoice list\n- Draft invoices excluded\n- All invoice statuses included (issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- Sorting by rate descending\n- Aggregating multiple lines with same rate\n- Aggregating multiple invoices\n- Base calculation with discounts\n- Zero VAT rate\n- Multiple VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n- Return structure validation\n- Input non-mutation\n- VAT calculation correctness\n\nAll 235 tests pass \u2713 (221 existing + 14 new VAT summary tests)",
